{
  "_comment": "Theme registry for chromaticli. Bundled themes use exact lowercase chromaticli <color-id> picker labels. Existing terminal RGB palettes are retained from the former upstream mappings; vscode.legacy_theme_ids recognizes those workspace labels read-only. Bundled workbench and syntax definitions are original chromaticli designs, not copies of upstream editor themes. New terminal palettes are original and may be tuned for readability and distinct color identity. themes.json owns background, foreground, cursor and all 16 ANSI colors; scripts/generate-vscode-themes.py copies them exactly into local theme files. After registry edits run python3 scripts/generate-vscode-themes.py, then python3 scripts/verify-themes.py before python3 scripts/generate-preview.py. Marketplace entries still require live verification. Keep registry and generated artifacts together.",
